  "Question": "The table below gives corresponding values of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) for a function: when \\(x=-2,-1,0,1,2\\), \\(y=3,0,-1,0,3\\), respectively. If \\(y=x^2+c\\), find the value of \\(y\\) when \\(x=3\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "8",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "When \\(x=0\\), \\(y=c=-1\\) (this is also verified by \\(4+c=3\\) when \\(x=-2\\)). Thus, \\(y=x^2-1\\), and when \\(x=3\\), \\(y=9-1=8\\).",
